# Archive artifacts are hash-verified. Preserve their bytes exactly.
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout and every
# line in paper/osf_upload/SHA256SUMS.txt stops verifying.
paper/osf_upload/** -text

# Same argument for the submission's supplementary package: it ships its own
# SHA256SUMS.txt and `sha256sum -c` must pass on a fresh checkout. With
# core.autocrlf=true (this machine) a text-mode checkout rewrites every CSV
# to CRLF, changing every recorded hash. Verified 2026-09-17: the package
# had no rule here and its SHA256SUMS.txt was itself CRLF, so
# `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt` failed on all 155 lines.
paper/submission/** -text
